course: dictionary
lesson: 7764
title: Sounds that tell a story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can be a sound as well as a thing. «Purr» is one of those words. When a cat purrs, it makes a low, soft, rumbling sound in its throat. A purr can be a noun too, as in «a soft purr».
explain: Context tells you what a purr means in each story. In Alice's story, Dinah is «purring so nicely by the fire», so the purr sounds calm and cosy. Cats often purr when they are content, but the sentence about hurt or scared cats warns you that a purr is not always a happy sign.
explain: Machines can purr too. An engine that purrs is running quietly and smoothly, with a steady, humming sound. The clue is the sound: a purr is soft and smooth, not loud and bumpy.
fact: «Purr» means a low, soft, rumbling sound, usually made by a cat.
fact: A «purr» can also be the sound itself, as in «a soft purr».
fact: An engine «purrs» when it makes a quiet, smooth humming sound.
fact: Cats purr when content, but sometimes also when hurt or scared.
fact: Look at the words around «purr» to find out whether it shows happiness, pain, or a smooth engine.
exercise: Alice's Dinah is «purring so nicely by the fire». What is a purr? | A loud shout | A bright light from the fire | *A low, soft, rumbling sound a cat makes, often when happy | A loud bang like a door slamming
exercise: «A dog may wag because it is nervous, and a cat may purr because it is hurt.» Why can a purr not always mean happy? | *Because cats also purr when hurt or scared | Because cats never feel anything at all | Because purring only happens at night
exercise: Which thing might purr? | A tap dripping in a sink | A kettle screaming on the stove | *A car engine running quietly and smoothly | A loud drum in a band
test: Look at «purr with pleasure». What does the phrase suggest? | A cat is angry and shouting | A cat is asleep under the bed | *A cat feels happy and content | A cat is lost outside
test: What word class is «purr» in «a soft purr»? | A question word | A verb | An adjective | *A noun
exam: Kittens knead their mother's tummy, and cats purr when content but sometimes also when hurt or scared: what should you check before deciding a purr means happiness? | *Check the words and clues around the purr | Check whether the cat is known for meowing | Check the colour of the cat | Check how many legs the cat has
